Colonel David "The Revenant" Rand was born and raised in the northern California Redwood Country, where even in 2319 a man can disappear into the woods. He is the son of a former US Army Special Forces Master Sergeant/CIA Special Activities Center operative, turned wilderness survivalist after becoming jaded with his government. David's father raised him like you think a former special operations soldier/wilderness survivalist would, as Survivors and Thinkers, including things like The "I Do, We Do, You Do" Method, After Action Reviews, Cooper’s Color Codes, PACE Planning, "The Look", Field Medicine, Land Navigation, Applied Science, and normal wilderness survival skills.
 While David was an exceptionally bright student growing up he often had difficulty 'fitting in' at school because the school taught 'conformity and mediocrity' in the words of his father. He was, however, an exceptional athlete that helped lead his high school to three state football championships and was a two time state wrestling champion. Between his decent 3.6 GPA and his athletic skills he was given a full scholarship to Stanford University where he played as a Defensive Lineman and won a NCAA Wrestling Championship before dropping out to join the Army with an 18-Xray contract his junior year.
 In his early days in the US army David received extensive training such as Ranger school, SF Assistant Operations/Intel Sergeant training, SERE Level C, Military Freefall, Special Operations Target Interdiction, and Environmental Reconnaissance. During his 6 years in the Army he continued his college education in his downtime, eventually earning degrees in Geophysics & Geospatial Intelligence. 
 Upon finishing his contract in the Army, and after earning his degrees he attended OCS and moved to the US Colonial Marines, where he became a Planetary Reconnaissance Officer within the 4th Marine Expeditionary Brigade, and within a relatively short period rose to the rank of Captain. During this time he also earned both a M.S. in Xenogeology & Resource Logistics and a B.A. War Studies which eventually led to the CIA’s Special Activities Center (SAC) within their Special Operations Group (SOG). As a USMC/CIA operative he became the man the Agency sent when diplomacy failed and a full-scale invasion was too messy. Whether it was neutralizing a bioweapon lab on a high-gravity 'Dry World' or conducting a deep-space boarding action on a hijacked freighter. It was his success in these 'off-the-books' conflicts, specifically his ability to secure vital resources in hostile territory without starting a regional war, that saw him fast-tracked through the field grades to the rank of Colonel. During these years he also earned his P.H.D in Planetology with the CIA's sponsorship.
 After a long and storied career in US special operations David was recruited to lead a UNMC unit often referred to in hushed tones as 'Vanguard Zero.' This was an organization designed to operate outside the friction of planetary bureaucracies, dealing specifically with 'systemic' threats that national governments couldn't touch. As the commanding officer of Vanguard Zero, David’s 'Troubleshooter' status was codified. He was given a Letter of Marque from the United Nations Security Council, authorizing him to secure humanity’s future by any means necessary. It was during these "black-tier" operations, surviving atmospheric re-entries in failing pods and emerging from the radioactive dust of "dead" worlds to complete his objective, that his moniker, "The Revenant," became a legend. He was the man who always came back, no matter the odds.
 When the Odyssey-01 mission needed a Mission Commander the UN practically demanded Colonel Rand fill that role, and despite him no longer working for the United States government, they accepted.
